                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "de082537-3ac8-3c47-8ebe-35691721d6a9",
                                        "entry_id": "ffec45d2-1fb6-32de-9456-cb2bd3ee54dd",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Initialism of sexually transmitted infection (also S.T.I.)."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "abbreviation",
                                            "alt-of",
                                            "initialism"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "4df1bc01-2388-4e60-91fc-82bb0f2e58f4",
                                                "sense_id": "de082537-3ac8-3c47-8ebe-35691721d6a9",
                                                "text": "For example, in the US army during the 21 months of the war that they were involved in, 6·8 million man days were lost due to STIs, and more than 10% of all disease admissions were for STIs."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "2e119b68-fca9-4faa-888b-4be60561127d",
                                                "sense_id": "de082537-3ac8-3c47-8ebe-35691721d6a9",
                                                "text": "This, of course, is something only people with that STI would know. For example, herpes is 437737."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "bc36e03b-33b0-471a-8c5c-56219b45d92f",
                                                "sense_id": "de082537-3ac8-3c47-8ebe-35691721d6a9",
                                                "text": "Although both acute PID and STIs may remain asymptomatic, some of their shared long-term sequelae are tubal factor infertility (TFI), salpingitis, and adhesions and scarring of the fallopian tubes, ovaries, and surrounding peritoneal tissue. These sequelae have been further identified as factors potentially associated with EOC risk."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
